From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PS3 Linux project <ps3@localhost>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 02:30:00 +0300
Subject: powerpc/ps3: don't pause a thread with an interrupt already pending

ps3_power_save() calls lv1_pause(0) soft-disabled, with MSR[EE] on. A
decrementer that fires between the idle loop's local_irq_disable() and the
hcall is masked: masked_interrupt sets DEC to 0x7fffffff (27 s at the
79.8 MHz timebase) and records PACA_IRQ_DEC for the replay. The thread then
pauses with no decrementer to wake it, and every timer queued on it (the
tick, hrtimers, timer-wheel timers) waits for the next external interrupt.
Thread 0 gets the device interrupts (PS3_BINDING_CPU_ANY binds them all to
it) and recovers within milliseconds; thread 1 gets only IPIs and can stay
asleep for seconds. On the PS3 this shows as games freezing for 0.3-4 s
with the CPU idle: ps3rsx's fence poll is an hrtimer on the waiter's CPU
(docs/STALLS.md "The recorder removes stalls").

Use prep_irq_for_idle() as pseries_lpar_idle() and the native Cell's
cbe_power_save() do: hard-disable, return without pausing when something
was masked (the replay in local_irq_enable() runs it), otherwise mark the
thread soft-enabled. Then hard-enable and pause with MSR[EE] on, the state
the hcall is normally entered in today, so from the check on a decrementer
or IPI is taken as a normal interrupt and re-arms the decrementer instead
of being masked.

Pausing with MSR[EE] off (prep_irq_for_idle_irqsoff(), as powernv does)
would close the last window too, but it relies on lv1_pause() ending on a
decrementer that is pending while MSR[EE] is off, and on the hypervisor
leaving that exception pending for the guest; neither is documented beyond
"MSR[EE] has no effect", and if either fails every idle thread loses its
tick. With MSR[EE] on, the one race left is an interrupt handled between
the hard-enable and the hcall: one that set need_resched is caught by the
check just before lv1_pause(), and otherwise the pause ends at the next
timer event (at most one tick with the periodic tick), not seconds later.

Forwarded: not yet (test on the PS3 first)

diff --git a/arch/powerpc/platforms/ps3/setup.c b/arch/powerpc/platforms/ps3/setup.c
--- a/arch/powerpc/platforms/ps3/setup.c
+++ b/arch/powerpc/platforms/ps3/setup.c
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
 #include <linux/cma.h>
 #include <linux/sizes.h>
 #include <linux/of.h>
+#include <linux/sched.h>
 
 #include <asm/machdep.h>
 #include <asm/firmware.h>
@@ -66,9 +67,36 @@ static void ps3_power_save(void)
 	 * lv1_pause() puts the PPE thread into inactive state until an
 	 * irq on an unmasked plug exists. MSR[EE] has no effect.
 	 * flags: 0 = wake on DEC interrupt, 1 = ignore DEC interrupt.
+	 *
+	 * The idle loop calls us soft-disabled with MSR[EE] on. A
+	 * decrementer that fires in that state is masked: the masked
+	 * handler pushes DEC out to 0x7fffffff (27 s at the 79.8 MHz
+	 * timebase) and leaves PACA_IRQ_DEC for the replay, so a pause
+	 * entered after it sleeps through every timer of this thread until
+	 * some other interrupt comes. The second thread gets nothing but
+	 * IPIs (all device interrupts are bound to thread 0).
+	 *
+	 * prep_irq_for_idle() hard-disables and returns false when
+	 * anything was masked since local_irq_disable(); the replay in
+	 * local_irq_enable() then runs it. Otherwise it marks us
+	 * soft-enabled, and we pause with MSR[EE] on, the state lv1_pause()
+	 * is normally called in: a decrementer or IPI from here on is
+	 * taken as a normal interrupt (the decrementer is re-armed), not
+	 * masked. This doesn't depend on whether the pause also ends on a
+	 * decrementer that is pending with MSR[EE] off. Unlike H_CEDE the
+	 * hcall doesn't enable MSR[EE] itself, so an interrupt can still be
+	 * handled just before it; one that made a task runnable here is
+	 * caught by the need_resched() check, and anything later than that
+	 * waits at most until the next timer event, never for a decrementer
+	 * that was pushed out.
 	 */
+	if (!prep_irq_for_idle())
+		return;
+
+	__hard_irq_enable();
 
-	lv1_pause(0);
+	if (!need_resched())
+		lv1_pause(0);
 }
 
 static void __noreturn ps3_restart(char *cmd)
